From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 16:44:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] MP3PLAY: the FILELEN worker gets off the JIT's core

It is created from inside a NatFeat, i.e. on the CPU thread, which is
pinned to core 2 at SCHED_FIFO 99 - and a new thread inherits both. So
it only ever ran when the CPU thread blocked: a folder's lengths came
minutes late and all at once, whenever the guest happened to go idle.
Same escape as avrecord's writer thread: normal class, low priority,
off cores 0 (render), 2 (JIT) and 3 (IPL poller). The log line goes to
stderr, where VGAPROF already is.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MGcLwq6U6E1QhD3W3PzuF7
---
 platforms/atari/audio/dmasnd_hdmi.c | 30 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 29 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/platforms/atari/audio/dmasnd_hdmi.c b/platforms/atari/audio/dmasnd_hdmi.c
index 3ddba1a..322161b 100755
--- a/platforms/atari/audio/dmasnd_hdmi.c
+++ b/platforms/atari/audio/dmasnd_hdmi.c
@@ -616,6 +616,8 @@ static long filelen_sync(const char *host_path)
  */
 #include <pthread.h>
 #include <time.h>
+#include <sched.h>
+#include <sys/resource.h>
 
 #define FL_SLOTS 64
 #define FL_PATH  528                        /* HOSTFS_HOST_PATH_MAX + 16 */
@@ -635,6 +637,32 @@ static unsigned long   fl_clock = 0;
 static void *fl_worker(void *arg)
 {
     (void)arg;
+
+    /* Created from inside a NatFeat, i.e. on the JIT's CPU thread - which
+     * is pinned to core 2 at SCHED_FIFO 99, and a new thread inherits
+     * both. Left like that, this worker only ever ran when the CPU thread
+     * blocked: lengths arrived minutes late and all at once, when the
+     * guest happened to go idle. Same escape as avrecord's writer: normal
+     * class, low priority, off cores 0 (render), 2 (JIT), 3 (IPL poller). */
+    {
+        cpu_set_t set;
+        struct sched_param sp;
+        long n = sysconf(_SC_NPROCESSORS_CONF);
+        long i;
+
+        CPU_ZERO(&set);
+        if (n < 1) n = 4;
+        for (i = 0; i < n && i < CPU_SETSIZE; i++)
+            if (i != 2 && !(n >= 4 && (i == 0 || i == 3)))
+                CPU_SET((int)i, &set);
+        if (CPU_COUNT(&set) == 0)
+            CPU_SET(0, &set);
+        sched_setaffinity(0, sizeof(set), &set);
+        memset(&sp, 0, sizeof(sp));
+        sched_setscheduler(0, SCHED_OTHER, &sp);
+        setpriority(PRIO_PROCESS, 0, 10);
+    }
+
     for (;;) {
         char path[FL_PATH];
         int i, pick = -1;
@@ -663,7 +691,7 @@ static void *fl_worker(void *arg)
             /* one line per file: what it answered and how long the read
              * took - a slow share shows up here as seconds per file, a
              * file it cannot open as -1 */
-            printf("[MP3] filelen %s -> %ld s (%ld ms)\n",
+            fprintf(stderr, "[MP3] filelen %s -> %ld s (%ld ms)\n",
                    base ? base + 1 : path, secs, ms);
             /* stdout is a pipe under systemd (the journal), so glibc
              * buffers it 4 KB at a time and a line like this would sit
